dy_ends\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span><span class=\"keyword\">val</span> body_ends : \u000A  <span><a href=\"../../arrayjit/Ir/Low_level/Access_fold/index.html#type-scopes\">LL.Access_fold.scopes</a> <span class=\"arrow\">&#45;&gt;</span></span>\u000A  <span><a href=\"../../arrayjit/Ir/Low_level/index.html#type-t\">LL.t</a> <span class=\"arrow\">&#45;&gt;</span></span>\u000A  <span><span class=\"xref-unresolved\">Base</span>.String.t <span class=\"arrow\">&#45;&gt;</span></span>\u000A  <span><span>(<span class=\"xref-unresolved\">Base</span>.int * <span>int <span class=\"xref-unresolved\">Base</span>.Option.t</span>)</span> <span class=\"xref-unresolved\">Base</span>.List.t</span></span></code></div><div class=\"spec-doc\"><p>The scope bodies of <code>llc</code> as <code>Access_fold</code> walks them under <code>local_scopes</code>, each when its walk ends -- a body ends after the definitions nested in it -- paired with the line of <code>source</code> holding its last assignment (<code>None</code>: no line assigns it). Pass the tree that renders: under <code>Emitted</code>, the one <a href=\"../../arrayjit/Ir/C_syntax/index.html#val-scope_order_oracles\"><code>Ir.C_syntax.scope_order_oracles</code></a> recorded (after the exact-scope collapse), so that every body it holds is in the text.</p></div></div><div class=\"odoc-spec\"><div class=\"spec value anchored\" id=\"val-in_text_order\"><a href=\"#val-in_text_order\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span><span class=\"keyword\">val</span> in_text_order : \u000A  <span><span><span>(<span class=\"xref-unresolved\">Base</span>.Int.t * <span><span class=\"xref-unresolved\">Base</span>.Int.t <span class=\"xref-unresolved\">Base</span>.Option.t</span>)</span> <span class=\"xref-unresolved\">Base</span>.List.t</span> <span class=\"arrow\">&#45;&gt;</span></span>\u000A  <span class=\"xref-unresolved\">Base</span>.bool</span></code></div><div class=\"spec-doc\"><p>Every body found in the text, each once, and in text order.</p></div></div><div class=\"odoc-spec\"><div class=\"spec value anchored\" id=\"val-reads_ahead_of_definition\"><a href=\"#val-reads_ahead_of_definition\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span><span class=\"keyword\">val</span> reads_ahead_of_definition : <span><span class=\"xref-unresolved\">Base</span>.String.t <span class=\"arrow\">&#45;&gt;</span></span> <span><span class=\"xref-unresolved\">Base</span>.Int.t <span class=\"arrow\">&#45;&gt;</span></span> <span>int <span class=\"xref-unresolved\">Base</span>.List.t</span></span></code></div><div class=\"spec-doc\"><p>The lines of <code>source</code> reading scope <code>id</code>'s local ahead of its last assignment: empty where the text defines the local before anything reads it. A local the text never assigns has every read ahead of it.</p></div></div><div class=\"odoc-spec\"><div class=\"spec value anchored\" id=\"val-names_local\"><a href=\"#val-names_local\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span><span class=\"keyword\">val</span> names_local : <span><span class=\"xref-unresolved\">Base</span>.String.t <span class=\"arrow\">&#45;&gt;</span></span> <span><span class=\"xref-unresolved\">Base</span>.Int.t <span class=\"arrow\">&#45;&gt;</span></span> bool</span></code></div><div class=\"spec-doc\"><p>Whether <code>source</code> names scope <code>id</code>'s local at all.</p></div></div>"}